# Tests that fail through dcfs on xfs, each with the reason: one "generic/NNN <reason>"
# per line (guest/xfstests.sh, xfstests_lib.sh). The run fails on a failure that is not listed,
# on a listed test that passes, does not run or times out. Reasons that name README.md point
# at the sentence that documents the behavior; "dcfs bug" is a finding for plan step 17.2
# (run FallocateFd, WriteFile and CopyFileRangeFd as the caller), fixed with a test first.
# Tests that take most of the limit or more are in xfstests.slow, tests that cannot run in
# this guest in xfstests.excluded; the tests that are "not run" are in xfstests.xfs.notrun.
generic/080 the mtime and ctime of a file written through a shared mmap are stale after close() (README.md: writes through a shared writable mmap after the last close() are seen late)
generic/215 the mtime and ctime of a file written through a shared mmap are stale after close() (README.md: writes through a shared writable mmap after the last close() are seen late)
generic/277 the kernel serves the previous ctime after chattr until the attribute timeout (README.md: after chattr through dcfs the kernel may serve the previous ctime)
generic/294 `mount -o remount,ro` is ignored by dcfs (dcfs.ro is the way to make the dcfs mount read-only; README.md, limitations: remount,ro and statx attributes), so touch on the "read-only" mount succeeds
generic/306 `mount -o remount,ro` is ignored by dcfs (dcfs.ro is the way to make the dcfs mount read-only; README.md, limitations: remount,ro and statx attributes), so touch on the "read-only" mount succeeds
generic/424 statx(2) does not report the append, immutable, nodump and compressed attributes that chattr set: FUSE has no way to carry them (README.md, limitations: remount,ro and statx attributes)
generic/732 the test mounts the scratch device twice (two mount points); dcfs refuses a second daemon on one cache database ("in use by another dcfs process"), README.md, limitations: a second dcfs needs its own cache database
